bool BHV_Survey::setParam(string param, string val)
{
  param = tolower(param);

  if((param == "survey_radius") && isNumber(val)) {
    double radius = atof(val.c_str());

    if(radius > 0) {
      m_radius = radius;
      return true;
    }
  }

  return false;
}

The MOOS-IvP-specific reason is that setParam() is not just a normal setter. It is part of the helm’s .bhv parsing contract.

When pHelmIvP reads a behavior block, it first tries to parse common behavior parameters through the IvPBehavior superclass, such as name, condition, priority, flags, duration, and related general behavior settings. If the superclass does not handle the parameter, the helm passes the parameter-value pair to your behavior’s local setParam() implementation. The MOOS-IvP documentation explicitly describes this superclass-first, subclass-second parsing pattern. 
